 2. ☕️🌯 Report: Starbucks mulls Chipotle bid 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios Chipotle shares jumped today after the Financial Times reported that Starbucks has considered acquiring the burrito chain, Axios' Nathan Bomey writes. 

 It's unclear whether an offer has been made or if it's just under consideration. Starbucks CEO Brian Niccol was widely credited with turning around Chipotle before taking on his current job, where he's been tasked with another revival effort.

 The move would rank as the biggest acquisition in the history of the restaurant industry by a long shot, topping Burger King's $11 billion deal for Tim Hortons in 2014. Go deeper . 

 
 
