 4. 📺 1 for the road: What to watch this weekend 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Whether you crave horror, thriller, comedy or sci-fi, there's a new streaming pick for you this weekend, Axios' Carly Mallenbaum writes. 

 😱 Carrie (Prime Video) 

 Mike Flanagan's adaptation of Stephen King's novel follows Carrie White (Summer H. Howell), a sheltered teen who faces a viral bullying scandal at her new school and discovers telekinetic powers. 👽 Disclosure Day (Peacock) 

 A Kansas City meteorologist (Emily Blunt) and a cybersecurity whistleblower (Josh O'Connor) race to reveal evidence of extraterrestrial life and a decades-long cover-up. 🪄 Small Prophets (Apple TV) 

 Seven years after his partner Clea disappears, Michael Sleep (Pearce Quigley) follows an alchemy recipe his father gave him to create magical spirits that can predict the future. More recs . 

 
 
